# Render API key, for scripts/render_teardown.sh. COPY THIS FILE TO `.env.render` AND PASTE THE
# KEY THERE -- `.env.render` is gitignored (`.env.*` in .gitignore), this file is not.
#
#   Render dashboard -> Account Settings -> API Keys -> Create API Key
#   cp .env.render.example .env.render
#   $EDITOR .env.render          # paste the key, save
#   bash scripts/render_teardown.sh
#
# The script lists every resource it found and requires you to type DELETE before removing
# anything. The key is read into the process environment only -- never echoed, never passed as a
# command-line argument (argv is visible in `ps`), never written anywhere else.
#
# THIS IS IRREVERSIBLE. A deleted Render Postgres is gone with its data. The dashboard's Postgres
# page has a "Download backup" action if you want a dump first.

RENDER_API_KEY=
